"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, accessibility, and data visualization through AI algorithms. The project was announced for initiation in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. Key phases include design, development (led by Omar Jensen), and compliance. The team has expanded with new members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Milestones include a successful prototype test for secure file sharing ahead of schedule, with UI enhancements planned for October. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase. Budgets have been approved for training ($15,000) and compliance ($55,000). A meeting to discuss initial findings is scheduled for August 5th."
